  "plan": {
    "goal": "Reproduce mid-range arterial wall shear stress of 1.5 Pa (15 dyn/cm²) in a perfused microfluidic channel.",
    "rationale": "Arterial wall shear stress ranges roughly 1–7 Pa (10–70 dyn/cm²); 1.5 Pa is a mid-range arterial value. Using the wide-rectangular-channel relation tau = 6·mu·Q/(w·h²), a 400 µm × 100 µm channel at 60 µL/min with water-like medium (mu = 1e-3 Pa·s) yields exactly 1.5 Pa. This geometry is a standard OOC footprint and the flow is within syringe-pump range. Reynolds number ≈ 4 (deeply laminar), pressure drop ≈ 600 Pa (0.6 kPa, trivial for a syringe pump), and residence time ≈ 0.8 s. Note: 1.5 Pa exceeds the HUVEC microvascular reference range (0.1–1.0 Pa), which is expected for an arterial (not microvascular) target; endothelial cells tolerate this range but it should be confirmed for the specific line.",
